From d1fec88a98bd43601d1deecac6fef093f215251f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:27:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(post): a turning section on a mill-turn needs a
 turning post

Maintainer's decision on PR #1265 (2026-11-12, "Refuse it"): a section
that turns the work - a turning op or an on-centre drill, as
lathe_voice::voice_of reads it - posts only through a post whose
dialect is turning (work_voice WorkSpindle). On a lathe or a mill-turn
a milling post would write it for the tool spindle; it is now refused
by name on every post path, nothing written. Milling and C-axis
sections on a mill-turn still post through a milling post; the shipped
Mill-turn machine's default post is unchanged.

- posting_serves::refusal takes the world and, when the kind is
  served, refuses the work-spindle sections a non-turning post would
  write (one derivation for lathe and mill-turn).
- lathe_workholding_mill_post: the mill-turn facing pin is now a
  refusal (stricter): refused by name at the chuck limit too.
- post_serves_kind: a mill-turn facing op through Haas (own post) and
  Fanuc (document post) is refused on post_mounts, post_per_op and
  post_setup; a turning post serves it.
- lathe_cross_drill: the generate-only tests stay on the plain lathe;
  only the posting test uses a mill-turn (review blocker 3).
- lathe_work_spindle: the on-centre drill on a mill-turn through the
  Fanuc mill post is now refused by name (was: posts).
- lathe_stroke: the built-in Mill-turn's turning job selects Fanuc
  Lathe, as the built-in Lathe's does.
- turning_contour_stock: indent (review note).

Refs #1232

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
